        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.37,
            0.882,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find out if you can reach the Sun in a lifetime, if you travel 1000 kilometers every day. (You had written down the distance between the Earth and the Sun in a previous exercise.)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.429,
            0.88,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We cannot reach the sun in a lifetime because it takes approx. 403 years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.481,
            0.881,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make necessary reasonable assumptions and answer the questions below:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.52,
            0.865,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) If a single sheet of paper weighs 5 grams, could you lift one lakh sheets of paper together at the same time?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.579,
            0.882,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Weight of one lakh (1,00,000) sheets = 500 kg. Since a person cannot lift 500 kg so, we cannot lift one lakh sheets of paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.651,
            0.822,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) If 250 babies are born every minute across the world, will a million babies be born in a day?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.69,
            0.68,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Babies born in one day = 3,60,000 babies. 3,60,000 is less than one million (10 lakh) Hence, a million babies cannot born in a day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.749,
            0.859,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) Can you count 1 million coins in a day? Assume you can count 1 coin every second.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.788,
            0.669,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " No. Because, Coins counted per day = 86,400"
            }
          ]
        },
